## Inline Explanation Rule — MANDATORY, line-by-line

Every method/function body MUST be densely commented: a `//` comment on **every
meaningful line or small block** explaining the *logic* — the **why**, what a
branch guards, why an order matters, what an edge case/magic value means — NOT a
restatement of the syntax. This is a hard requirement ("have to"); a bare line
of non-trivial logic with no comment fails review. Applies to services,
processors, resolvers, utils — all code bodies.

```ts
// load the subscription row — counters + window timestamps live here
const sub = await this.entityManager.findOne(AiSubscriptionEntity, { where: { userId } })

// no row yet → user never provisioned; fall back to the free Auto lane
if (!sub) {
    return this.provisionFreeLane(userId)
}

// roll the 5h window forward when the stored window has expired
if (this.isWindowExpired(sub.window5hResetAt)) {
    sub.used5h = 0                          // reset per-window counter
    sub.window5hResetAt = this.next5hBoundary() // stamp next rollover
}

// reject early when the spend would exceed the remaining quota
if (sub.used5h + cost > sub.limit5h) {
    throw new AiQuotaExceededException({ userId }) // typed code for callers to branch on
}
```

Do NOT restate syntax (`// increment i` over `i++` is noise) — explain intent
(`// skip disabled keys so the rotator never hands one out`). Loops,
conditionals, early-returns, and try/catch each get a lead comment.

